@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Concurrent motion · reproduced GIGA communication failure
caption Motor-disconnected application fixture; this is an unresolved qualification blocker.
footer Temporal sequence from console records; the exact blocking / scheduling mechanism is not yet established.
autonumber
actor CLI
box "M7 · UI" #EDF4FE
participant "Client / Planner" as C
participant "ICC Bridge / Application" as U
end box
boundary "Shared-memory transport" as T #FFF5DF
box "M4 · IO" #EAF7F4
participant "ICC / Server" as S
participant "Controller / Executor" as E
end box
CLI -> C : axis jog shoulder -.2 --continuous
C -> U : acquire, prepare, run
U -> T : serialized messages
T -> S : deliver
S -> E : start rolling shoulder program
E --> C : Running (through ICC)
CLI -> C : axis move elbow -1
C -> U : acquire / prepare / run independent axis
U -> T : serialized messages
T -> S : deliver
S -> E : start independent elbow program
E --> C : Running (through ICC)
note over U,E #FFF5DF
  Both jobs are legal members of the Axis family.
  Heartbeats and ownership renewals must remain serviceable.
end note
U -> U : peer heartbeat deadline expires
U -> U : report "Peer heartbeat expired"\nrequest application shutdown
U --x C : ownership renewal can no longer complete
C -> C : retain uncertainty about remote execution
E -> E : apply local ownership / link-loss handling
note over S,E #FFF5DF
  No HardFault observed; M4 remains alive.
  A short debugger sample found command serialization active,
  but does not prove that serialization caused the timeout.
end note
note over CLI,E #FFF0F1
  Passing isolated raw / coordinated waveform captures do not
  qualify this overlap. Do not claim complete application readiness.
  No relaxation of heartbeat or ownership deadlines was applied.
end note
@enduml
